      "text": "    provider = provider or os.environ.get(\"SPECSTRIDE_DSH_PROVIDER\", \"\") or \"openrouter\"",
      "why": "the conflict under test needs a DSH provider in the environment AND a model ref that embeds a different one. The as-is variable that names the DSH provider (`SPECSTRIDE_DSH_PROVIDER`, `SPECSTRIDE_DSH_CRITIC_PROVIDER`) stands in the environment alias table of feature 100, annex X \u00a7X.8 in PROSE only ('The as-is variables of one harness for its home, its provider and the provider of its critic'), so `hermeticEnvironment` cannot declare it and the fixture cannot set it. The edit supplies the value the variable would, and nothing else: the conflict itself is raised by the model ref the fixture declares, at the line under test (`lib/critic.py:1963`). The port reaches the same state through `harnesses.dsh.provider` and takes no edit."
    }
